From: CachyOS-ARM64 port overlay <builder@local>
Date: Wed, 08 Oct 2026
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: hamoa-pmics: include spmi-vadc.h for ADC5_GEN3_VPH_PWR

hamoa-pmics.dtsi uses PM8550_ADC5_GEN3_VPH_PWR(1), which expands to
((sid) << 8 | ADC5_GEN3_VPH_PWR). The bare ADC5_GEN3_VPH_PWR constant
(0x8e) lives in dt-bindings/iio/adc/qcom,spmi-vadc.h, which this file
never included, so cpp leaves the token unexpanded and dtc fails with:

  Lexical error: arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/hamoa-pmics.dtsi:290.24-41
  Unexpected 'ADC5_GEN3_VPH_PWR'

Add the missing include. Verified value: channel node is channel@18e =
(1 << 8 | 0x8e), consistent with PM8550_ADC5_GEN3_VPH_PWR(1).
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/hamoa-pmics.dtsi | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/hamoa-pmics.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/hamoa-pmics.dtsi
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/hamoa-pmics.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/hamoa-pmics.dtsi
@@ -11,6 +11,7 @@
 #include <dt-bindings/pinctrl/qcom,pmic-gpio.h>
 #include <dt-bindings/spmi/spmi.h>
 #include "qcom-adc5-gen3.h"
+#include <dt-bindings/iio/adc/qcom,spmi-vadc.h>
 
 #define SID_BASE 0
